  "summary": "San Jose elected leaders, including Mayor Matt Mahan, unveiled proposed new safeguards for the city's ALPR program following public outcry over alleged misuse of the data. The proposal would restrict use of personal devices to access law enforcement data, expand audits for illicit searches, and push for state legislation stiffening penalties for improper handling of ALPR data.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Facing public outcry over alleged misuse of San Jose's automated license plate reader data, a group of elected leaders has unveiled new safeguards for the controversial technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "They would also expand audits designed to catch elicit searches.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    }
